implementationPlan.description:
THE FLIP, AS ORDERED ARGV (DoD 4). Edit `apps/daemon/src/deployment/deploy-service.ts` and add the proxy-reload port to `apps/daemon/src/deployment/deploy-ports.ts`.

THE SEQUENCE, and the order IS the feature:
1. start the candidate INTERNAL (the service already does this and probes it by name);
2. rewrite the proxy upstream to the candidate;
3. RELOAD the proxy — the atomic instant;
4. ONLY AFTER the reload returns 0, stop the incumbent.

INVOCATION DISCIPLINE (DoD 4): bare `docker` under `shell: false` with an argv ARRAY. Never a hard-coded `.cmd` (the measured host returns EINVAL for one under shell:false), never a shell string, never a chain. The rewrite and the reload are each their own recorded call.

ADD NO MEMBER TO `moe-deploy-receipt/1` (rail 2). task-da60dc4b (rollback, WORKING) is building against the shape as it stands and resolves rollbacks through those receipts; a member added here is one that row has never seen.

If you introduce a layer stamp for the new refusal, NAME IT WITHOUT a `LAYER`/`LAYERS`/`BOUNDARIES` suffix, or leave it unexported and publish only `export type`. `tests/security/boundary-roster.security.ts:603` scans `^export const ([A-Z0-9_]+(?:LAYERS|LAYER|BOUNDARIES))` and a match owes a security-roster row plus cardinality pins that are foreign to this row. Prefer reusing an already-rostered literal.
